# The GitHub tokens `tart-runner` polls with, as `op://` references rather than
# values: the dispatcher resolves one on first use, into a shell variable that no
# child process of its own can read, and never into a file or an argument list.
# Nothing here is a secret, which is why it is tracked like any other config.
#
# One line per *owner*, not per repository, because a fine-grained personal access
# token is "limited to access resources owned by a single user or organization" —
# so repositories under two owners need two tokens, and the owner half of a line in
# ~/.config/tart-runner/repos is what picks the one to use. The suffix is the owner
# uppercased with anything but a letter or a digit turned into an underscore.
#
# The token itself is a fine-grained token with, on the listed repositories and
# nothing else, Administration: write (which mints and deletes just-in-time
# runners) and Actions: read (which lists runs and their jobs). Metadata: read
# comes with any of them. Deliberately not the account's `gh` login, which carries
# the `repo` scope and so every private repository there is. The repository README
# has the whole procedure, including what an organization has to allow first.
#
# The item this names does not exist yet: the runner is switched off, the
# repository list is empty, and nothing resolves a reference until a line is added
# to it.
TART_RUNNER_TOKEN_TIMCHE="op://Development/GitHub - tart-runner timche/token"
